    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (78.68) and **Junior Caminero** (76.88) serving as our undisputed anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start, leveraging an elite .444 xwOBA against a beatable Flaherty, while **Junior Caminero** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Kelly. We are also leaning heavily into speed-dependent upside today; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.03) is a priority play because he faces a slower-paced pitching environment that significantly boosts his steal probability, and **Trea Turner** (68.26) provides similar high-ceiling utility at the top of the order against a favorable platoon matchup. These players form the core of our strategy to maximize SB volume without sacrificing run-production efficiency.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Colt Keith** (52.08) and **Jacob Gonzalez** (44.32). While **Colt Keith** narrowly cleared the 40-point efficiency floor to remain in the utility slot, his score was suppressed by a poor 3.40 xERA matchup against Brown. **Jacob Gonzalez** was the strongest candidate to displace him, but his projected efficiency failed to surpass **Colt Keith**\u2019s platoon edge and favorable order placement. Meanwhile, we continue to keep **Dillon Dingler** (36.48) and **Carson Benge** (37.03) on the bench as their matchups against tough lefties\u2014Luzardo and Brown\u2014fall well below our operational threshold. We are monitoring **Christian Yelich** closely; despite his 55.76 score, his significant negative platoon adjustment (\u201313%) makes him our highest-risk start if his role atop the order shifts. As always, **Rece Hinds** remains unavailable due to his assignment in Jacksonville, and we will continue to manage our remaining depth pieces like **Hyeseong Kim**, **Zac Veen**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Luke Raley**, **Josh Smith**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Jose Fernandez**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena** based strictly on daily efficiency projections to preserve our game caps.",
